# ── raw sgit store files: opaque ciphertext, not text ─────────────────
# The encrypted vault store (.sg_vault/**, minus the gitignored local/)
# IS tracked in git — that is the point: the git remote holds a
# zero-knowledge mirror of the vault. Treat it as binary: no diffs, no
# merge attempts, no EOL normalisation. Ciphertext has no meaningful
# line-based diff, and a textual merge would corrupt it.
.sg_vault/** binary -diff -merge
obj-cas-imm-* binary -diff -merge
ref-pid-*     binary -diff -merge
idx-pid-*     binary -diff -merge
key-rnd-imm-* binary -diff -merge
branch-named-* binary -diff -merge
branch-clone-* binary -diff -merge

# ── generated pages: keep diffs quiet in PRs ──────────────────────────
# Every *.html is produced by admin/build/build_pages.py; mark it
# generated so code hosts collapse these diffs and reviewers look at the
# generator instead.
*.html linguist-generated=true
